rts REUSED_INSERT_THICKNESS_MISMATCH across all four RI-4 mosaic crates. Because the defect resides in a shared insert batch and requires scope-level disposition authority, the dossier is an architectural fail with bounded continuation for pedestal crates.\",\"earliestSharedCausalBoundary\":\"Use of the nonconforming RI-4 insert batch during construction of the four sealed mosaic crates.\",\"completeDefectClass\":\"REUSED_INSERT_THICKNESS_MISMATCH affecting every Sable mosaic crate mapped to RI-4.\",\"safeIndependentContinuation\":\"Release independently verified pedestal crates; their inserts, records, crews, and shipment releases are separate and they use no RI-4 material.\",\"retainedEvidenceSufficient\":true,\"repeatedLoopDetected\":false,\"smallestAdvancingAction\":\"Request bounded conservation authority for controlled RI-4 insert disposition across all four held mosaic crates; do not open crates or replace inserts unless that authority is granted.\",\"authorityClass\":\"BOUNDED_ENGINEERING\",\"authorizationBasis\":\"E06 authorizes holding the four mosaic crates, preserving window evidence, releasing verified pedestal crates, and requesting bounded insert disposition; H04 requires bounded conservation authority before opening or replacement.\",\"prohibitedOperations\":[\"Open a mosaic crate without granted bounded conservation authority.\",\"Replace an insert without granted authority.\",\"Declare HUMIDITY_CARD_DYE_VARIANCE as a historical recurrence.\",\"Hold independently verified pedestal crates without evidence.\"],\"uncertainties\":[\"The condition of the sealed mosaics is unknown.\",\"The mechanism producing the installed-card blotching is not established.\",\"The final controlled rework or insert-disposition method requires bounded conservation authority.\"],\"boundedRationaleSummary\":\"Direct thickness and ledger evidence establish a shared RI"
